/-!
# Hash map lemmas: `filterMap`, `filter`, `map`

Std's `Std/Data/HashMap/Lemmas.lean`, lines 3076-3580, with Std's statements, attributes and
commands; the proofs are generated from Std's proof chain (`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` §6.2). Where no
generated proof compiled, the proof was written by hand (`tools/data/hand.json`):
`filterMap_equiv_filter`, `keys_filter`, `filterMap_equiv_map`, `getElem?_map`, `getElem_map`,
`getElem!_map` and `getD_map`. `filterMap_equiv_filter` and `filterMap_equiv_map` go through the
model, because Std's proofs use Raw₀'s map equalities `filterMap_eq_filter` and `filterMap_eq_map`,
which we do not have. `keys_filter` is Std's proof with the map argument given explicitly. In Std's
order the `LawfulBEq` lemmas `getElem?_map`, `getElem_map`, `getElem!_map` and `getD_map` come
before the primed lemmas their DHashMap proofs cite, so the first two are proved from the model and
the other two from `getElem?_map`.

Generated by `tools/port.py lemmas` from Std v4.35.0 and `tools/data/hand.json`; edit those,
not this file (`tools/ci.sh` checks that regenerating reproduces it).

Owner: PORT (Wave 1), LEM-7 (Wave 2).
-/

set_option linter.missingDocs true
set_option autoImplicit false

universe u v w w'

variable {α : Type u} {β : Type v} {γ : Type w} {δ : Type w'} {_ : BEq α} {_ : Hashable α}

namespace SwissTable.HashMap

